Then I see a man.
He is going for a walk with a dog.
I go to the man.
"Excuse me, please," I say.
The man stops.
"Yes, please?" he asks kindly.
"I am looking for Museum Island," I say.
"How do I get to Museum Island?"
The man smiles.
"That is quite easy," he says.
"First go to the crossing."
"Then turn left."
"Keep going straight to the water."
"You see the museums there."
"Thank you very much," I say.
"You are welcome," the man answers.
I set off to the crossing.
